    "title": "Natura 2000 end-2024",
    "description": "All 11 layers of the source EEA Natura2000_end2024.gpkg (the boundary-polygon layer plus 10 non-spatial lookup tables: SPECIES, HABITATS, DESIGNATIONSTATUS, HABITATCLASS, BIOREGION, IMPACT, MANAGEMENT, OTHERSPECIES, METADATA, NATURA2000SITES), each exported to its own Parquet/GeoParquet file. Unlike an earlier polygon-only export, this item makes every layer independently accessible, joinable on SITECODE.",
    "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
    "sci:doi": "10.2909/91357f39-7866-41ce-b447-43905c364ec8",
    "sci:citation": "European Environment Agency (2025). Natura 2000 (vector), version end 2024, edition 01.00. Dataset code eea_v_3035_100_k_natura2000_p_2024_v01_r00. https://doi.org/10.2909/91357f39-7866-41ce-b447-43905c364ec8",
    "processing:lineage": "Exported from the source EEA GeoPackage (Natura2000_end2024.gpkg, dataset code eea_v_3035_100_k_natura2000_p_2024_v01_r00) via the BMD workflow engine, one Parquet file per GeoPackage layer (11 total) rather than a single combined file. The NaturaSite_polygon layer was written with geopandas 1.1.4, with added xmin/ymin/xmax/ymax covering columns for row-group pruning; CRS (EPSG:3035) and geometry are unchanged from source. Verification status: row count (27173) and CRS/bbox for NaturaSite_polygon match an earlier, separately-produced single-layer polygon export that WAS independently verified against the source GeoPackage (row count via pyogrio.read_info(), plus exact attribute/geometry checks on two sites, SITECODE NL3009017 and AT1101112) — but this specific file differs in size from that earlier export (~1008MB vs ~1094MB, consistent with a different geopandas version and the added covering columns), so it has not itself been independently re-verified byte-for-byte. The other 10 non-spatial tables have not yet been independently verified in this process at all; row counts and columns below are as reported by the export pipeline, not independently checked against the source.",
    "table:primary_geometry": "geometry"
  },
